# Web Up: "When this enchantment enters, exile target nonland permanent an opponent controls until this enchantment leaves the
# battlefield" (CR 610.3). On turn three its trigger offers Bot2's Ornithopter and not Bot1's own Ornithopter or Bot2's Plains
# (the refusals, beside the positive control of the Ornithopter that is chosen). On turn four Bot2's Disenchant destroys Web Up and
# the exiled Ornithopter comes back to the battlefield under its owner's control, a new object (summoning sick).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Web Up
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Disenchant
Ornithopter
Plains x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#3.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Web Up.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Plains)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Pearl
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Web Up)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Web Up
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Pearl; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.SummoningSick = true
